// A `@target(.X)` body whose name matches no bare `@target` declaration.
//
// The plan calls for R2036 here — a body must belong to exactly one group — on
// the grounds that a typo in the name is the mistake users will make most often.
// That diagnostic is NOT implemented, and this fixture records what happens
// instead: the orphan becomes its OWN declaration, valid on its target and
// absent elsewhere.
//
// That is not silence — W0007 catches the typo, because nothing calls the
// misspelled name. It is a weaker net than R2036 (it fires only when the orphan
// is also unused, and it is a warning), but it is a net. Pinning it here means
// implementing R2036 later will show up as a snapshot change rather than a
// surprise.

module "main"

@target
export platform_name :: fn() -> string = "posix"

main :: fn() -> i32 = 0
